-- | A genesis, guardian-governance-owned token registry: 'NttCoin' (a
-- 'Holding'), 'NttCoinFactory' (a genesis 'BurnMintFactory' plus, for
-- CIP-0056/CIP-0112 compliance, 'TransferFactory' v1+v2), and the supporting
-- transfer-side templates 'TransferPreapproval'/'NttTransferInstruction'. All
-- in one module: Daml requires an interface instance to live in either the
-- interface's or the implementing template's own module, and 'NttCoinFactory'
-- implements interfaces (BurnMintFactory, TransferFactory v1/v2) whose
-- helper logic needs to create/inspect 'NttCoin' -- splitting the transfer
-- helpers into a separate module that both defines and is imported by this
-- one is a genuine module cycle, not just a style choice.
--
-- Modeled on Canton Coin's @AmuletRules@/@Amulet@: 'NttCoinFactory' is
-- @signatory guardianGovernance@ alone, created once at genesis by the same
-- k-of-n guardian-quorum flow that creates 'Wormhole.Ntt.Governance.NttGovernance',
-- and never replaced -- it carries no mutable config, so there is nothing to
-- rotate the way @AmuletRules_SetConfig@ rotates Amulet's fee schedule. If a
-- gg-administered deployment ever needs a different factory, the existing
-- 'Wormhole.Ntt.Manager.NttManager' choice @SetFactory@ (already co-signed by
-- @effectiveMinter@) re-points at a new cid.
--
-- Unlike Amulet -- which has exactly one instrument per @dso@ and so can
-- derive @instrumentId@ from @dso@ alone -- one @guardianGovernance@ here
-- administers many distinct instruments (each deployment's registering admin
-- binds its own @instrumentId.id@; only @instrumentId.admin@ is shared), so
-- 'NttCoin' stores @instrumentId@ directly rather than deriving it, and
-- 'NttCoinFactory' is generic over it: its only invariant is
-- @instrumentId.admin == guardianGovernance@, checked on every burn/mint or
-- transfer.
--
-- 'BurnMintFactory_BurnMint' is jointly controlled by @(view this).admin ::
-- extraActors@ (the interface's own spec). Every real caller in this codebase
-- (the outbound-burn 'Wormhole.Ntt.Manager.BurnMintMinterProxy' and the
-- inbound-mint 'Wormhole.Ntt.Deposit.DepositPreapproval.Deposit') already
-- includes each output's owner in @extraActors@, so 'NttCoin's
-- @(instrumentId.admin, owner)@ signatories are always satisfiable with no
-- extra plumbing.
--
-- @TransferFactory_Transfer@'s v1 controller is @transfer.sender@ alone (v2:
-- caller-chosen @actors@) -- no receiver, no admin. Since 'NttCoin' is
-- @signatory instrumentId.admin, owner, provider (if any)@, creating the
-- receiver's new holding needs the receiver's (and its provider's) own
-- authority, which isn't ambiently present. This is
-- resolved the same way real Canton Coin does: a three-way branch on (1)
-- self-transfer / v2 actors already including the receiver (their authority
-- is already present), (2) the receiver has a standing 'TransferPreapproval'
-- (a self-signed side contract whose choice inherits the receiver's
-- authority, exactly like 'Wormhole.Ntt.Deposit.DepositPreapproval' does for
-- burn/mint deposits), or (3) neither -- lock the sender's funds now and
-- create a 'NttTransferInstruction' the receiver accepts (or rejects) later.
--
-- Account model (CIP-0112): 'NttCoin' supports the full 'HoldingV2.Account'
-- model on both sides of every v2 path (ordinary transfers, preapprovals,
-- pending instructions, and v2 allocations) -- provider-delegated accounts
-- and sub-accounts (@id /= ""@) are genuine, composable holdings, not merely
-- tolerated inputs. Only the null-owner account (@owner = None@) is rejected
-- by @TransferFactory@/@AllocationFactory@ v2 (see 'requireAccountOwner'):
-- the standard reserves null-owner accounts for mint/burn, and bridge
-- mint/burn is routed through @BurnMintFactory@ as a deliberate,
-- spec-compliant scope boundary (CIP-0112 permits but never mandates routing
-- mint/burn through the standard transfer/allocation interfaces). That said,
-- @BurnMintFactory@ is NOT the only code path that can create a holding
-- without an in-choice debit: 'TransferPreapproval_Receive' is a second,
-- gg-only mint primitive (controller @instrumentId.admin@ alone) -- it is
-- debit-balanced only because 'nttTransferCore' debits the sender first in
-- the same transaction; invoked standalone it is an unbacked mint. It is
-- gated on gg alone, though -- the instrument's mint authority -- so it is no
-- more privileged than @BurnMintFactory@ itself, and is therefore acceptable;
-- it just means bridge mint/burn is not, as previously stated here, the sole
-- mint path. v1 has no
-- account concept at all, so v1 paths (and 'BurnMintFactory_BurnMint') stay
-- basic-account-only (@provider = None, accountId = ""@) by construction --
-- not a limitation, just v1's own scope.
--
-- Authority invariant: creating or archiving any 'NttCoin' requires
-- @instrumentId.admin :: owner :: provider (if any)@ -- enforced by the
-- template's own @signatory@ clause regardless of which interface view a
-- caller reaches it through (see 'accountControlParties'). A
-- provider-managed coin is therefore never spendable without the provider's
-- authority actually present in the transaction; a v1-only caller that lacks
-- a provider's authority simply cannot move a provider-managed coin -- safe,
-- just unusable via v1, which is the intended restriction (v1 has no
-- provider concept to begin with).
--
-- Locks: the v2 'HoldingV2.Holding' view's @lock@ is always @None@ --
-- 'NttCoin' has no lock-creating consumer, and the standard treats locks as
-- optional (there is no standard interface choice to "lock a holding"). This
-- is a deliberate, spec-compliant scope decision, not a gap: escrow/DvP needs
-- are already served by allocations (v2 net settlement, below) and, at the
-- manager layer, by @LockedLedger@. A full lock lifecycle, if ever needed,
-- is a separate feature.
--
-- == Allocation v2 / SettlementFactory
--
-- A v2 'AV2.Allocation' only ever authorizes ONE party's (the @authorizer@'s)
-- side of possibly many legs -- unlike v1 (one contract = one full
-- sender-to-receiver leg), a real transfer between two parties always needs
-- TWO allocations (the sender's, with a @SenderSide@ leg; the receiver's,
-- with a matching @ReceiverSide@ leg). 'Allocation_Settle' on a single
-- allocation can therefore never move value between parties by itself: each
-- allocation's own settle only ever touches its own legs (decrementing its
-- own locked bookkeeping for @SenderSide@ legs -- the real value already
-- left circulation at allocate time; creating a fresh holding for itself for
-- @ReceiverSide@ legs, using authority inherited from its own signatories).
-- Soundness -- that every debit is matched by exactly one credit of the same
-- amount -- depends entirely on 'SettlementFactory_SettleBatch' validating
-- that every leg's both sides are present and consistent BEFORE
-- nested-exercising each allocation's own settle in the same transaction.
-- 'SettlementFactory_SettleBatch' is therefore the thing that makes the v2
-- model sound at all, not just a batching convenience; a direct
-- 'Allocation_Settle' call outside it remains possible (required for
-- interface conformance) but is an expert/unsafe escape hatch with no
-- automatic counterparty -- this factory does not special-case or block it,
-- since there is nothing an individual allocation could mechanically check.
-- (It does, however, apply a caller-forgeable footgun guard against
-- *accidental* naked calls -- see 'settleBatchContextKey' -- which is
-- deliberately not a security control, since the real authorization is the
-- @admin :: executors@ actors requirement on the choice itself.)
--
-- Iterated settlement: an allocation's @transferLegSides@ are a STANDING
-- authorization, not a one-shot one -- they recur on every settlement
-- iteration for as long as the allocation keeps carrying forward. A
-- 'FinalizedAllocation.extraTransferLegSides' passed at settle time is
-- purely additive on top of those standing legs for that one iteration; it
-- never replaces or disables them. This is the intended
-- reusable/recurring-allocation model (e.g. a standing weekly payment leg
-- that keeps firing each settlement round) and is conservation-safe by
-- construction, since every iteration's settle still separately balances its
-- own sender/receiver totals against its own locked bookkeeping. The
-- executor chooses @nextIterationFunding@ at settle time (bounded by what
-- remains locked after that round's spend) to fund the following round's
-- standing legs; it is the executor's responsibility to carry forward enough
-- to cover them -- an undersized carry simply aborts the next settle
-- (insufficient locked balance), and the funds are never stranded: they
-- remain recoverable via 'Allocation_Withdraw' (once any settlement deadline
-- has passed, for committed allocations) or 'Allocation_Cancel'.
module Wormhole.Ntt.Coin where

import DA.Action (when)
import DA.Foldable (forA_)
import DA.List (dedup)
import DA.Map qualified as Map
import DA.Optional (catOptionals, fromOptional, fromSome, isNone, isSome, optionalToList)
import DA.TextMap qualified as TextMap

import Splice.Api.Token.HoldingV1 (Holding, HoldingView (..), InstrumentId (..))
import Splice.Api.Token.HoldingV2 qualified as HoldingV2
import Splice.Api.Token.MetadataV1 (AnyValue (..), ExtraArgs (..), emptyMetadata)
import Splice.Api.Token.BurnMintV1
  ( BurnMintFactory, BurnMintFactoryView (..)
  , BurnMintFactory_BurnMintResult (..)
  )
import Splice.Api.Token.TransferInstructionV1 qualified as TIV1
import Splice.Api.Token.TransferInstructionV2 qualified as TIV2
import Splice.Api.Token.AllocationV1
import Splice.Api.Token.AllocationInstructionV1
import Splice.Api.Token.AllocationV2 qualified as AV2
import Splice.Api.Token.AllocationInstructionV2 qualified as AIV2

template NttCoin
  with
    instrumentId : InstrumentId
    owner        : Party
    provider     : Optional Party
    accountId    : Text
    amount       : Decimal
  where
    signatory instrumentId.admin :: owner :: optionalToList provider
    -- Strictly positive, matching Canton Coin's own holdings (Amulet requires
    -- initialAmount > 0.0; Chainlink's CoinHolding uses > 0.0) -- a zero-amount
    -- holding is dust with no economic meaning, so it is rejected outright
    -- rather than tolerated on-ledger.
    ensure amount > 0.0

    -- v1 has no provider/sub-account concept, so the v1 view is always the
    -- bare owner -- callers reaching a provider-managed or sub-account coin
    -- through v1 still see it (visibility is unaffected), they just can't
    -- move it without the provider's authority (see module header).
    interface instance Holding for NttCoin where
      view = HoldingView with
        owner
        instrumentId
        amount
        lock = None
        meta = emptyMetadata

    interface instance HoldingV2.Holding for NttCoin where
      view = HoldingV2.HoldingView with
        account = coinAccount owner provider accountId
        instrumentId = HoldingV2.InstrumentId with admin = instrumentId.admin, id = instrumentId.id
        amount
        lock = None
        meta = emptyMetadata

----------------------------------------------------------------------
-- Transfer-side helpers and templates
----------------------------------------------------------------------

-- | Build a full 'HoldingV2.Account' from its three constituent parts.
coinAccount : Party -> Optional Party -> Text -> HoldingV2.Account
coinAccount owner provider accountId = HoldingV2.Account with owner = Some owner, provider, id = accountId

-- | A basic account: a plain party, no sub-account, no provider delegation.
-- Used by every v1 (and 'BurnMintFactory_BurnMint') path, which has no
-- account concept of its own -- see module header.
basicAccountV2 : Party -> HoldingV2.Account
basicAccountV2 p = HoldingV2.Account with owner = Some p, provider = None, id = ""

-- | The parties whose authority is required to move or archive a holding
-- held in this account: the owner (always, once past the null-owner check
-- below) plus the provider, if any. Mirrors 'NttCoin's own @signatory@
-- clause -- see module header's authority invariant.
accountControlParties : HoldingV2.Account -> [Party]
accountControlParties acc = catOptionals [acc.owner, acc.provider]

-- | 'NttCoinFactory's @TransferFactory@/@AllocationFactory@ v2 accept any
-- account except the null-owner one -- see module header. Sub-accounts
-- (@id /= ""@) and provider-delegated accounts are genuine, composable
-- accounts, not rejected.
requireAccountOwner : HoldingV2.Account -> Update Party
requireAccountOwner acc = case acc.owner of
  Some p -> pure p
  None -> abort "ntt: null-owner accounts are for mint/burn only -- use BurnMintFactory"

-- | The @extraArgs.context@ key a caller uses to pass a receiver's standing
-- 'TransferPreapproval' cid through to 'transferFactory_transferImpl' -- the
-- interface's choice arguments are fixed, so there's no dedicated field for
-- it. Absent or undecodable falls back to the pending path (fail-safe: a
-- caller who doesn't know about this never gets a transfer mis-credited).
transferPreapprovalContextKey : Text
transferPreapprovalContextKey = "ntt.transferPreapprovalCid"

lookupTransferPreapprovalCid : ExtraArgs -> Optional (ContractId TransferPreapproval)
lookupTransferPreapprovalCid extraArgs =
  case TextMap.lookup transferPreapprovalContextKey extraArgs.context.values of
    Some (AV_ContractId cid) -> Some (coerceContractId cid)
    _ -> None

-- | A recipient's standing, self-signed consent to receive ordinary
-- transfers of one instrument -- the transfer-side analog of
-- 'Wormhole.Ntt.Deposit.DepositPreapproval'.
template TransferPreapproval
  with
    account      : HoldingV2.Account
    instrumentId : InstrumentId
  where
    signatory accountControlParties account
    observer instrumentId.admin

    -- Standalone, this is a gg-only unbacked mint -- acceptable only because
    -- gg is already the instrument's mint authority. It conserves value (is
    -- debit-balanced) only when driven from 'nttTransferCore', which debits
    -- the sender before reaching this choice in the same transaction.
    nonconsuming choice TransferPreapproval_Receive : ContractId Holding
      with
        receiver             : HoldingV2.Account
        amount               : Decimal
        expectedInstrumentId : InstrumentId
      controller instrumentId.admin
      do
        assertMsg "ntt: preapproval owner is not this transfer's receiver" (receiver == account)
        assertMsg "ntt: preapproval instrument does not match the requested instrumentId"
          (expectedInstrumentId == instrumentId)
        toInterfaceContractId @Holding <$> create NttCoin with
          instrumentId, owner = fromSome account.owner, provider = account.provider, accountId = account.id, amount

-- | The pending state of an in-flight transfer with no standing preapproval:
-- funds are already debited from the sender (archived + change returned) by
-- the time this is created; it holds the value directly rather than
-- referencing a separate locked holding, since nothing else here needs to
-- reuse a "locked coin" concept. Implements both v1 and v2 @TransferInstruction@
-- on one template (mirroring how real Canton Coin's own
-- @AmuletTransferInstruction@ implements both versions on a single contract).
template NttTransferInstruction
  with
    instrumentId    : InstrumentId
    senderAccount   : HoldingV2.Account   -- ^ owner is always @Some@ -- null-owner rejected upstream
    receiverAccount : HoldingV2.Account   -- ^ owner is always @Some@ -- null-owner rejected upstream
    amount          : Decimal
    requestedAt     : Time
    executeBefore   : Time
  where
    signatory instrumentId.admin :: accountControlParties senderAccount
    observer accountControlParties receiverAccount

    interface instance TIV1.TransferInstruction for NttTransferInstruction where
      view = TIV1.TransferInstructionView with
        originalInstructionCid = None
        transfer = TIV1.Transfer with
          sender = fromSome senderAccount.owner
          receiver = fromSome receiverAccount.owner
          amount, instrumentId, requestedAt, executeBefore
          inputHoldingCids = []
          meta = emptyMetadata
        status = TIV1.TransferPendingReceiverAcceptance
        meta = emptyMetadata

      transferInstruction_acceptImpl _self _arg = do
        now <- getTime
        assertMsg "ntt: transfer.executeBefore has passed; accept is no longer allowed -- reject or withdraw"
          (now < executeBefore)
        rcid <- toInterfaceContractId @Holding <$> create NttCoin with
          instrumentId, owner = fromSome receiverAccount.owner
          provider = receiverAccount.provider, accountId = receiverAccount.id, amount
        pure TIV1.TransferInstructionResult with
          output = TIV1.TransferInstructionResult_Completed with receiverHoldingCids = [rcid]
          senderChangeCids = []
          meta = emptyMetadata

      transferInstruction_rejectImpl _self _arg = returnToSenderV1 instrumentId senderAccount amount
      transferInstruction_withdrawImpl _self _arg = returnToSenderV1 instrumentId senderAccount amount
      transferInstruction_updateImpl _self _arg =
        abort "ntt: NttTransferInstruction does not support registry-internal Update steps"

    interface instance TIV2.TransferInstruction for NttTransferInstruction where
      view = TIV2.TransferInstructionView with
        originalInstructionCid = None
        transfer = TIV2.Transfer with
          sender = senderAccount, receiver = receiverAccount, amount
          instrumentId = HoldingV2.InstrumentId with admin = instrumentId.admin, id = instrumentId.id
          requestedAt, executeBefore
          inputHoldingCids = []
          meta = emptyMetadata
        expiresAt = None
        availableActions = Map.fromList
          [ (TIV2.TIA_Accept, [accountControlParties receiverAccount])
          , (TIV2.TIA_Reject, [accountControlParties receiverAccount])
          , (TIV2.TIA_Withdraw, [accountControlParties senderAccount])
          ]
        meta = emptyMetadata

      transferInstruction_acceptImpl self _arg = do
        now <- getTime
        assertMsg "ntt: transfer.executeBefore has passed; accept is no longer allowed -- reject or withdraw"
          (now < executeBefore)
        rcid <- toInterfaceContractId @HoldingV2.Holding <$> create NttCoin with
          instrumentId, owner = fromSome receiverAccount.owner
          provider = receiverAccount.provider, accountId = receiverAccount.id, amount
        -- TransferInstructionV2's TransferInstruction_Accept is nonconsuming --
        -- the interface MANDATES the instruction be archived on acceptance (see
        -- module header / Phase 1 finding 1A); v1's own Accept is a plain
        -- (consuming) choice, so it needs no explicit archive.
        archive (coerceContractId @TIV2.TransferInstruction @NttTransferInstruction self)
        pure TIV2.TransferInstructionResult with
          output = TIV2.TransferInstructionResult_Completed with receiverHoldingCids = [rcid]
          senderChangeCids = []
          meta = emptyMetadata

      transferInstruction_rejectImpl self arg = do
        assertMsg "ntt: TransferInstruction_Reject requires the recipient account's authority"
          (all (`elem` arg.actors) (accountControlParties receiverAccount))
        result <- returnToSenderV2 instrumentId senderAccount amount
        archive (coerceContractId @TIV2.TransferInstruction @NttTransferInstruction self)
        pure result

      transferInstruction_withdrawImpl self arg = do
        assertMsg "ntt: TransferInstruction_Withdraw requires the sender account's authority"
          (all (`elem` arg.actors) (accountControlParties senderAccount))
        result <- returnToSenderV2 instrumentId senderAccount amount
        archive (coerceContractId @TIV2.TransferInstruction @NttTransferInstruction self)
        pure result

      transferInstruction_acceptExtraObservers _ = []
      transferInstruction_rejectExtraObservers _ = []
      transferInstruction_withdrawExtraObservers _ = []

-- | Both 'TIV1.TransferFactory_Transfer' and 'TIV2.TransferFactory_Transfer'
-- state that the choice MUST fail if @transfer.executeBefore@ is in the past;
-- v2's @Transfer.requestedAt@ additionally MUST be in the past when
-- instructing. Shared so both @transferFactory_transferImpl@s enforce the
-- exact same window (Phase 1 finding 1B).
assertTransferWindow : Time -> Time -> Update ()
assertTransferWindow requestedAt executeBefore = do
  now <- getTime
  assertMsg "ntt: transfer.requestedAt must not be in the future" (requestedAt <= now)
  assertMsg "ntt: transfer.executeBefore has passed" (now < executeBefore)

returnToSenderV1 : InstrumentId -> HoldingV2.Account -> Decimal -> Update TIV1.TransferInstructionResult
returnToSenderV1 instrumentId senderAccount amount = do
  cid <- toInterfaceContractId @Holding <$> create NttCoin with
    instrumentId, owner = fromSome senderAccount.owner
    provider = senderAccount.provider, accountId = senderAccount.id, amount
  pure TIV1.TransferInstructionResult with
    output = TIV1.TransferInstructionResult_Failed
    senderChangeCids = [cid]
    meta = emptyMetadata

returnToSenderV2 : InstrumentId -> HoldingV2.Account -> Decimal -> Update TIV2.TransferInstructionResult
returnToSenderV2 instrumentId senderAccount amount = do
  cid <- toInterfaceContractId @HoldingV2.Holding <$> create NttCoin with
    instrumentId, owner = fromSome senderAccount.owner
    provider = senderAccount.provider, accountId = senderAccount.id, amount
  pure TIV2.TransferInstructionResult with
    output = TIV2.TransferInstructionResult_Failed
    senderChangeCids = [cid]
    meta = emptyMetadata

-- | The shared value-movement core for 'NttCoinFactory's @TransferFactory@
-- v1 and v2 @transferFactory_transferImpl@s: validates and archives the
-- sender's inputs, mints exact + change, then completes synchronously
-- (self-transfer, or receiver authority already present, or a standing
-- preapproval) or falls through to the pending case -- the caller
-- constructs the actual 'NttTransferInstruction' (it alone has the original,
-- version-specific 'TIV1.Transfer'/'TIV2.Transfer' fields to store). Takes
-- full 'HoldingV2.Account's rather than bare parties so it can move value on
-- behalf of provider-delegated/sub-accounts on either side (Phase 2) -- the
-- caller has already run 'requireAccountOwner' on both accounts, so
-- @senderAccount.owner@/@receiverAccount.owner@ are guaranteed @Some@ here.
data CoreTransferOutcome
  = CoreCompleted with receiverCid : ContractId Holding, senderChangeCids : [ContractId Holding]
  | CorePendingNeeded with senderChangeCids : [ContractId Holding]

nttTransferCore
  : Party -> Bool -> HoldingV2.Account -> HoldingV2.Account -> Decimal -> InstrumentId -> [ContractId Holding] -> ExtraArgs
  -> Update CoreTransferOutcome
nttTransferCore guardianGovernance receiverAuthorityPresent senderAccount receiverAccount amount instrumentId inputHoldingCids extraArgs = do
  assertMsg "ntt: NttCoinFactory only serves instruments administered by guardianGovernance"
    (instrumentId.admin == guardianGovernance)
  assertMsg "ntt: transfer amount must be positive" (amount > 0.0)
  let sender = fromSome senderAccount.owner
  views <- forA inputHoldingCids (fmap view . fetch)
  forA_ views \hv -> do
    assertMsg "ntt: transfer input not owned by sender" (hv.owner == sender)
    assertMsg "ntt: transfer input instrument mismatch" (hv.instrumentId == instrumentId)
  let total = sum (map (.amount) views)
  assertMsg "ntt: input holdings do not cover the transfer amount" (total >= amount)
  forA_ inputHoldingCids archive
  let change = total - amount
  senderChangeCids <-
    if change > 0.0
      then do
        cid <- toInterfaceContractId @Holding <$> create NttCoin with
          instrumentId, owner = sender, provider = senderAccount.provider, accountId = senderAccount.id, amount = change
        pure [cid]
      else pure []
  if receiverAuthorityPresent
    then do
      rcid <- toInterfaceContractId @Holding <$> create NttCoin with
        instrumentId, owner = fromSome receiverAccount.owner
        provider = receiverAccount.provider, accountId = receiverAccount.id, amount
      pure CoreCompleted with receiverCid = rcid, senderChangeCids
    else case lookupTransferPreapprovalCid extraArgs of
      Some preCid -> do
        rcid <- exercise preCid TransferPreapproval_Receive with
          receiver = receiverAccount, amount, expectedInstrumentId = instrumentId
        pure CoreCompleted with receiverCid = rcid, senderChangeCids
      None -> pure CorePendingNeeded with senderChangeCids

----------------------------------------------------------------------
-- NttCoinFactory
----------------------------------------------------------------------

template NttCoinFactory
  with
    guardianGovernance : Party
  where
    signatory guardianGovernance

    interface instance BurnMintFactory for NttCoinFactory where
      view = BurnMintFactoryView with admin = guardianGovernance, meta = emptyMetadata

      burnMintFactory_burnMintImpl _self arg = do
        assertMsg "ntt: NttCoinFactory only serves instruments administered by guardianGovernance"
          (arg.instrumentId.admin == guardianGovernance)
        assertMsg "ntt: expectedAdmin does not match this factory's admin"
          (arg.expectedAdmin == guardianGovernance)
        forA_ arg.inputHoldingCids \cid -> do
          hv <- view <$> fetch cid
          assertMsg "ntt: burn input's instrument does not match the requested instrumentId"
            (hv.instrumentId == arg.instrumentId)
          archive cid
        -- BurnMintFactory is party-based, not account-based -- mint/burn stays
        -- basic-account-only by construction (see module header).
        outputCids <- forA arg.outputs \o ->
          toInterfaceContractId @Holding <$> create NttCoin with
            instrumentId = arg.instrumentId
            owner = o.owner
            provider = None, accountId = ""
            amount = o.amount
        pure BurnMintFactory_BurnMintResult with outputCids

      burnMintFactory_publicFetchImpl _self arg = do
        assertMsg "ntt: expectedAdmin does not match this factory's admin"
          (arg.expectedAdmin == guardianGovernance)
        pure BurnMintFactoryView with admin = guardianGovernance, meta = emptyMetadata

    interface instance TIV1.TransferFactory for NttCoinFactory where
      view = TIV1.TransferFactoryView with admin = guardianGovernance, meta = emptyMetadata

      transferFactory_transferImpl _self arg = do
        assertMsg "ntt: expectedAdmin does not match this factory's admin"
          (arg.expectedAdmin == guardianGovernance)
        let t = arg.transfer
        assertTransferWindow t.requestedAt t.executeBefore
        -- v1 is inherently basic (a bare party, no account model) -- lift
        -- the sender/receiver parties into basic accounts for the shared,
        -- account-based core (Phase 2).
        let senderAccount = basicAccountV2 t.sender
            receiverAccount = basicAccountV2 t.receiver
        outcome <- nttTransferCore guardianGovernance (t.sender == t.receiver)
          senderAccount receiverAccount t.amount t.instrumentId t.inputHoldingCids arg.extraArgs
        case outcome of
          CoreCompleted{receiverCid, senderChangeCids} ->
            pure TIV1.TransferInstructionResult with
              output = TIV1.TransferInstructionResult_Completed with receiverHoldingCids = [receiverCid]
              senderChangeCids
              meta = emptyMetadata
          CorePendingNeeded{senderChangeCids} -> do
            instructionCid <- create NttTransferInstruction with
              instrumentId = t.instrumentId, senderAccount, receiverAccount, amount = t.amount
              requestedAt = t.requestedAt, executeBefore = t.executeBefore
            pure TIV1.TransferInstructionResult with
              output = TIV1.TransferInstructionResult_Pending with
                transferInstructionCid = toInterfaceContractId instructionCid
              senderChangeCids
              meta = emptyMetadata

      transferFactory_publicFetchImpl _self arg = do
        assertMsg "ntt: expectedAdmin does not match this factory's admin"
          (arg.expectedAdmin == guardianGovernance)
        pure TIV1.TransferFactoryView with admin = guardianGovernance, meta = emptyMetadata

    interface instance TIV2.TransferFactory for NttCoinFactory where
      view = TIV2.TransferFactoryView with admin = guardianGovernance, meta = emptyMetadata

      transferFactory_transferExtraObservers _ = []

      transferFactory_transferImpl _self arg = do
        let t = arg.transfer
        assertTransferWindow t.requestedAt t.executeBefore
        -- Only the null-owner account is rejected -- sub-accounts and
        -- provider-delegated accounts are genuine, composable accounts on
        -- both sides (Phase 2, module header).
        _ <- requireAccountOwner t.sender
        _ <- requireAccountOwner t.receiver
        assertMsg "ntt: TransferFactory_Transfer requires the sender account's owner and provider authority"
          (all (`elem` arg.actors) (accountControlParties t.sender))
        let instrumentId = InstrumentId with admin = t.instrumentId.admin, id = t.instrumentId.id
            inputHoldingCids = map coerceContractId t.inputHoldingCids
            receiverAuthorityPresent = all (`elem` arg.actors) (accountControlParties t.receiver)
        outcome <- nttTransferCore guardianGovernance receiverAuthorityPresent
          t.sender t.receiver t.amount instrumentId inputHoldingCids arg.extraArgs
        case outcome of
          CoreCompleted{receiverCid, senderChangeCids} ->
            pure TIV2.TransferInstructionResult with
              output = TIV2.TransferInstructionResult_Completed with
                receiverHoldingCids = [coerceContractId receiverCid]
              senderChangeCids = map coerceContractId senderChangeCids
              meta = emptyMetadata
          CorePendingNeeded{senderChangeCids} -> do
            instructionCid <- create NttTransferInstruction with
              instrumentId, senderAccount = t.sender, receiverAccount = t.receiver, amount = t.amount
              requestedAt = t.requestedAt, executeBefore = t.executeBefore
            pure TIV2.TransferInstructionResult with
              output = TIV2.TransferInstructionResult_Pending with
                transferInstructionCid = toInterfaceContractId instructionCid
              senderChangeCids = map coerceContractId senderChangeCids
              meta = emptyMetadata

      transferFactory_publicFetchImpl _self _arg =
        pure TIV2.TransferFactoryView with admin = guardianGovernance, meta = emptyMetadata

    interface instance AllocationFactory for NttCoinFactory where
      view = AllocationFactoryView with admin = guardianGovernance, meta = emptyMetadata

      allocationFactory_allocateImpl _self arg = do
        let spec = arg.allocation
            leg = spec.transferLeg
        assertMsg "ntt: NttCoinFactory only serves instruments administered by guardianGovernance"
          (leg.instrumentId.admin == guardianGovernance)
        assertMsg "ntt: expectedAdmin does not match this factory's admin"
          (arg.expectedAdmin == guardianGovernance)
        assertMsg "ntt: allocation amount must be positive" (leg.amount > 0.0)
        now <- getTime
        assertMsg "ntt: allocation window (allocateBefore) has passed" (now < spec.settlement.allocateBefore)
        views <- forA arg.inputHoldingCids (fmap view . fetch)
        forA_ views \hv -> do
          assertMsg "ntt: allocation input not owned by sender" (hv.owner == leg.sender)
          assertMsg "ntt: allocation input instrument mismatch" (hv.instrumentId == leg.instrumentId)
        let total = sum (map (.amount) views)
        assertMsg "ntt: input holdings do not cover the allocation amount" (total >= leg.amount)
        forA_ arg.inputHoldingCids archive
        let change = total - leg.amount
        senderChangeCids <-
          if change > 0.0
            then do
              -- v1 allocations are party-based, not account-based -- basic by
              -- construction (see module header).
              cid <- toInterfaceContractId @Holding <$> create NttCoin with
                instrumentId = leg.instrumentId, owner = leg.sender, provider = None, accountId = "", amount = change
              pure [cid]
            else pure []
        allocationCid <- toInterfaceContractId @Allocation <$> create NttCoinAllocation with
          instrumentId = leg.instrumentId, allocation = spec
        pure AllocationInstructionResult with
          output = AllocationInstructionResult_Completed with allocationCid
          senderChangeCids
          meta = emptyMetadata

      allocationFactory_publicFetchImpl _self arg = do
        assertMsg "ntt: expectedAdmin does not match this factory's admin"
          (arg.expectedAdmin == guardianGovernance)
        pure AllocationFactoryView with admin = guardianGovernance, meta = emptyMetadata

    interface instance AIV2.AllocationFactory for NttCoinFactory where
      view = AIV2.AllocationFactoryView with admin = guardianGovernance, meta = emptyMetadata

      allocationFactory_allocateExtraObservers _ = []

      allocationFactory_allocateImpl _self arg = do
        let spec = arg.allocation
        assertMsg "ntt: allocation's admin does not match this factory's admin"
          (spec.admin == guardianGovernance)
        -- Only the null-owner account is rejected -- a provider-delegated or
        -- sub-account authorizer is genuine and composable (Phase 2, module
        -- header); its owner AND provider must both authorize the allocate.
        _ <- requireAccountOwner spec.authorizer
        assertMsg "ntt: AllocationFactory_Allocate requires the authorizer account's owner and provider authority"
          (all (`elem` arg.actors) (accountControlParties spec.authorizer))
        assertMsg "ntt: transferLegSides amounts must be positive"
          (all (> 0.0) (map (.amount) spec.transferLegSides))
        assertMsg "ntt: nextIterationFunding amounts must be positive"
          (all ((> 0.0) . snd) (TextMap.toList (fromOptional TextMap.empty spec.nextIterationFunding)))

        now <- getTime
        let round1Totals = sumSide AV2.SenderSide spec.transferLegSides
            reserveTotals = fromOptional TextMap.empty spec.nextIterationFunding
            requiredTotals = textMapUnionWith (+) round1Totals reserveTotals

        inputViews <- forA arg.inputHoldingCids \cid -> do
          hv <- view <$> fetch cid
          assertMsg "ntt: allocation input not owned by the authorizer" (hv.account == spec.authorizer)
          assertMsg "ntt: allocation input's instrument admin does not match this factory's admin"
            (hv.instrumentId.admin == guardianGovernance)
          pure hv
        forA_ arg.inputHoldingCids archive
        let inputsByInstrument = TextMap.fromListWithR (+) [(hv.instrumentId.id, hv.amount) | hv <- inputViews]
            instruments = dedup (map fst (TextMap.toList requiredTotals) ++ map fst (TextMap.toList inputsByInstrument))

        results <- forA instruments \instr -> do
          let have = fromOptional 0.0 (TextMap.lookup instr inputsByInstrument)
              need = fromOptional 0.0 (TextMap.lookup instr requiredTotals)
          assertMsg ("ntt: input holdings for " <> instr <> " do not cover the allocation's required funding")
            (have >= need)
          let change = have - need
          changeCids <-
            if change > 0.0
              then do
                cid <- toInterfaceContractId @HoldingV2.Holding <$> create NttCoin with
                  instrumentId = InstrumentId with admin = guardianGovernance, id = instr
                  owner = fromSome spec.authorizer.owner
                  provider = spec.authorizer.provider, accountId = spec.authorizer.id, amount = change
                pure [cid]
              else pure []
          pure (instr, need, changeCids)

        allocationCid <- toInterfaceContractId @AV2.Allocation <$> create NttCoinAllocationV2 with
          authorizerAccount = spec.authorizer
          settlement = arg.settlement
          allocation = spec
          lockedAmounts = TextMap.filter (> 0.0) (TextMap.fromList [(i, n) | (i, n, _) <- results])
          originalAllocationCid = None
          createdAt = now
          numIterations = 0

        pure AIV2.AllocationInstructionResult with
          output = AIV2.AllocationInstructionResult_Completed with allocationCid
          authorizerChangeCids = TextMap.fromList [(i, cs) | (i, _, cs) <- results, not (null cs)]
          meta = emptyMetadata

      allocationFactory_publicFetchImpl _self _arg =
        pure AIV2.AllocationFactoryView with admin = guardianGovernance, meta = emptyMetadata

    interface instance AV2.SettlementFactory for NttCoinFactory where
      view = AV2.SettlementFactoryView with admin = guardianGovernance, meta = emptyMetadata

      settlementFactory_settleBatchExtraObservers _ = []

      settlementFactory_settleBatchImpl _self arg = do
        assertMsg "ntt: SettlementFactory_SettleBatch requires at least one transfer leg"
          (not (null arg.transferLegs))
        assertMsg "ntt: SettlementFactory_SettleBatch requires actors to be exactly settlement.executors"
          (sameGroup arg.actors arg.settlement.executors)
        assertMsg "ntt: duplicate transferLegId in transferLegs"
          (length (dedup (map (.transferLegId) arg.transferLegs)) == length arg.transferLegs)

        allocViews <- forA arg.allocations \fa -> do
          av <- view <$> fetch fa.allocationCid
          assertMsg "ntt: allocation's admin does not match this factory's admin"
            (av.allocation.admin == guardianGovernance)
          assertMsg "ntt: allocation was not created for this settlement" (av.settlement == arg.settlement)
          pure (fa, av)

        let entries =
              [ (s.transferLegId, s.side, av.allocation.authorizer, s.otherside, s.amount, s.instrumentId)
              | (fa, av) <- allocViews, s <- av.allocation.transferLegSides ++ fa.extraTransferLegSides
              ]

        forA_ arg.transferLegs \leg -> do
          let senders = [e | e@(tlid, AV2.SenderSide, _, _, _, _) <- entries, tlid == leg.transferLegId]
              receivers = [e | e@(tlid, AV2.ReceiverSide, _, _, _, _) <- entries, tlid == leg.transferLegId]
          assertMsg ("ntt: transferLeg " <> leg.transferLegId <> " has no matching SenderSide allocation")
            (length senders == 1)
          assertMsg ("ntt: transferLeg " <> leg.transferLegId <> " has no matching ReceiverSide allocation")
            (length receivers == 1)
          let [(_, _, sAuth, sOther, sAmt, sInstr)] = senders
              [(_, _, rAuth, rOther, rAmt, rInstr)] = receivers
          assertMsg ("ntt: transferLeg " <> leg.transferLegId <> " SenderSide authorization mismatch")
            (sAuth == leg.sender && sOther == leg.receiver && sAmt == leg.amount && sInstr == leg.instrumentId)
          assertMsg ("ntt: transferLeg " <> leg.transferLegId <> " ReceiverSide authorization mismatch")
            (rAuth == leg.receiver && rOther == leg.sender && rAmt == leg.amount && rInstr == leg.instrumentId)

        assertMsg "ntt: allocations authorize transfer leg sides not covered by the given transferLegs"
          (length entries == 2 * length arg.transferLegs)

        allocationSettleResults <- forA allocViews \(fa, _) ->
          exercise fa.allocationCid AV2.Allocation_Settle with
            actors = guardianGovernance :: arg.settlement.executors
            extraTransferLegSides = fa.extraTransferLegSides
            nextIterationFunding = fa.nextIterationFunding
            extraArgs = withSettleBatchContext arg.extraArgs

        pure AV2.SettlementFactory_SettleBatchResult with allocationSettleResults, meta = emptyMetadata

      settlementFactory_publicFetchImpl _self _arg =
        pure AV2.SettlementFactoryView with admin = guardianGovernance, meta = emptyMetadata

----------------------------------------------------------------------
-- Allocation v1: NttCoinAllocation
----------------------------------------------------------------------

-- | A single-contract allocation: value + the allocation record folded
-- together (spec-sanctioned -- 'AllocationView.holdingCids' MAY be empty for
-- registries that don't represent locked value as a separate on-ledger
-- holding). No separate locked-holding indirection, for the same reason as
-- 'NttTransferInstruction' -- nothing else here needs to reuse a "locked
-- coin" concept.
template NttCoinAllocation
  with
    instrumentId : InstrumentId
    allocation   : AllocationSpecification
  where
    signatory instrumentId.admin, allocation.transferLeg.sender
    observer allocation.transferLeg.receiver, allocation.settlement.executor

    interface instance Allocation for NttCoinAllocation where
      view = AllocationView with allocation, holdingCids = [], meta = emptyMetadata

      allocation_executeTransferImpl _self _arg = do
        now <- getTime
        assertMsg "ntt: settlement window (settleBefore) has passed" (now < allocation.settlement.settleBefore)
        rcid <- toInterfaceContractId @Holding <$> create NttCoin with
          instrumentId, owner = allocation.transferLeg.receiver, provider = None, accountId = ""
          amount = allocation.transferLeg.amount
        pure Allocation_ExecuteTransferResult with
          senderHoldingCids = [], receiverHoldingCids = [rcid], meta = emptyMetadata

      allocation_cancelImpl _self _arg = do
        cid <- returnAllocationToSender instrumentId allocation
        pure Allocation_CancelResult with senderHoldingCids = [cid], meta = emptyMetadata

      allocation_withdrawImpl _self _arg = do
        cid <- returnAllocationToSender instrumentId allocation
        pure Allocation_WithdrawResult with senderHoldingCids = [cid], meta = emptyMetadata

-- | v1 allocations are party-based, not account-based -- basic by
-- construction (see module header).
returnAllocationToSender : InstrumentId -> AllocationSpecification -> Update (ContractId Holding)
returnAllocationToSender instrumentId allocation =
  toInterfaceContractId @Holding <$> create NttCoin with
    instrumentId, owner = allocation.transferLeg.sender, provider = None, accountId = ""
    amount = allocation.transferLeg.amount

----------------------------------------------------------------------
-- Allocation v2: NttCoinAllocationV2 -- see module header for the
-- multi-leg/SettlementFactory soundness argument.
----------------------------------------------------------------------

sameGroup : [Party] -> [Party] -> Bool
sameGroup xs ys = all (`elem` ys) xs && all (`elem` xs) ys

-- | The @extraArgs.context@ key 'settlementFactory_settleBatchImpl' stamps
-- onto every nested @Allocation_Settle@ it exercises, so
-- 'allocation_settleImpl' can tell it was reached via
-- 'AV2.SettlementFactory_SettleBatch' rather than a direct call. This is a
-- footgun guard against an *accidental* naked @Allocation_Settle@ (which has
-- no automatic counterparty and so cannot itself check conservation), NOT a
-- security boundary -- the sentinel is caller-forgeable by anyone who already
-- holds the @admin :: executors@ authority the choice requires, exactly the
-- same parties who could authorize a real 'SettlementFactory_SettleBatch'
-- anyway. The actual authorization is, and remains, that
-- @Allocation_Settle@ requires the admin (gg) among @actors@ (see module
-- header).
settleBatchContextKey : Text
settleBatchContextKey = "ntt.viaSettleBatch"

-- | Insert the 1D sentinel into a caller-supplied 'ExtraArgs', preserving
-- whatever context values were already there.
withSettleBatchContext : ExtraArgs -> ExtraArgs
withSettleBatchContext extraArgs = extraArgs with
  context = extraArgs.context with
    values = TextMap.insert settleBatchContextKey (AV_Bool True) extraArgs.context.values

-- | 'DA.TextMap' has no @unionWith@/@map@ -- these are the two shapes this
-- module needs, built from the primitives it does export.
textMapUnionWith : (v -> v -> v) -> TextMap.TextMap v -> TextMap.TextMap v -> TextMap.TextMap v
textMapUnionWith f a b = TextMap.fromListWithR f (TextMap.toList a ++ TextMap.toList b)

textMapNegate : TextMap.TextMap Decimal -> TextMap.TextMap Decimal
textMapNegate m = TextMap.fromList [(k, negate v) | (k, v) <- TextMap.toList m]

sumSide : AV2.TransferSide -> [AV2.TransferLegSide] -> TextMap.TextMap Decimal
sumSide side sides = TextMap.fromListWithR (+) [(s.instrumentId, s.amount) | s <- sides, s.side == side]

-- | Otherside account control parties (owner, plus provider if present) of
-- the ORIGINAL transferLegSides, deduped. Gives counterparties -- and their
-- providers, who the standard requires have visibility on all asset
-- movements of their account -- standing ACS visibility of an allocation
-- naming them, generalizing v1's @observer allocation.transferLeg.receiver@
-- to multi-leg.
legSideOwners : [AV2.TransferLegSide] -> [Party]
legSideOwners sides = dedup (concatMap (accountControlParties . (.otherside)) sides)

returnLockedFundsToAuthorizerV2
  : Party -> HoldingV2.Account -> TextMap.TextMap Decimal -> Update (TextMap.TextMap [ContractId HoldingV2.Holding])
returnLockedFundsToAuthorizerV2 admin account amounts =
  TextMap.fromList <$> forA (filter ((> 0.0) . snd) (TextMap.toList amounts)) \(instr, amt) -> do
    cid <- toInterfaceContractId @HoldingV2.Holding <$> create NttCoin with
      instrumentId = InstrumentId with admin, id = instr
      owner = fromSome account.owner, provider = account.provider, accountId = account.id, amount = amt
    pure (instr, [cid])

-- | One authorizer's side of possibly many legs of a settlement -- see the
-- module header for why value only genuinely moves when
-- 'AV2.SettlementFactory_SettleBatch' settles matching sender/receiver
-- allocations together in one transaction. @lockedAmounts@ is bookkeeping
-- only (no separate escrow holding, same simplification as
-- 'NttCoinAllocation'/'NttTransferInstruction') -- the real value already
-- left circulation (archived) at 'AllocationFactory_Allocate' time.
template NttCoinAllocationV2
  with
    authorizerAccount     : HoldingV2.Account   -- ^ owner is always @Some@ -- null-owner rejected upstream
    settlement            : AV2.SettlementInfo
    allocation            : AV2.AllocationSpecification
    lockedAmounts         : TextMap.TextMap Decimal
    originalAllocationCid : Optional (ContractId AV2.Allocation)
    createdAt             : Time
    numIterations         : Int
  where
    signatory allocation.admin :: accountControlParties authorizerAccount
    observer settlement.executors, legSideOwners allocation.transferLegSides

    interface instance AV2.Allocation for NttCoinAllocationV2 where
      view = AV2.AllocationView with
        originalAllocationCid, settlement, allocation
        holdingCids = []
        createdAt, numIterations
        expiresAt = None
        availableActions = Map.fromList
          [ (AV2.AA_Settle, [allocation.admin :: settlement.executors])
          , (AV2.AA_Cancel, [settlement.executors, [allocation.admin]])
          , (AV2.AA_Withdraw, if allocation.committed then [] else [[fromSome authorizerAccount.owner]])
          ]
        meta = emptyMetadata

      allocation_settleImpl self arg = do
        assertMsg "ntt: Allocation_Settle requires exactly admin and executors as actors"
          (sameGroup arg.actors (allocation.admin :: settlement.executors))
        -- Footgun guard, not a security boundary -- see 'settleBatchContextKey'.
        assertMsg "ntt: Allocation_Settle must be driven through SettlementFactory_SettleBatch"
          (TextMap.lookup settleBatchContextKey arg.extraArgs.context.values == Some (AV_Bool True))
        now <- getTime
        forA_ allocation.settlementDeadline \deadline ->
          assertMsg "ntt: settlement deadline has passed" (now <= deadline)
        assertMsg "ntt: extraTransferLegSides/nextIterationFunding require iterated settlement to be enabled"
          ((null arg.extraTransferLegSides && isNone arg.nextIterationFunding) || isSome allocation.nextIterationFunding)
        assertMsg "ntt: extraTransferLegSides amounts must be positive"
          (all (> 0.0) (map (.amount) arg.extraTransferLegSides))

        let allSides = allocation.transferLegSides ++ arg.extraTransferLegSides
            senderTotals = sumSide AV2.SenderSide allSides
            receiverTotals = sumSide AV2.ReceiverSide allSides
        forA_ (TextMap.toList senderTotals) \(instr, amt) ->
          assertMsg ("ntt: locked " <> instr <> " balance does not cover this round's SenderSide legs")
            (fromOptional 0.0 (TextMap.lookup instr lockedAmounts) >= amt)
        let remaining = textMapUnionWith (+) lockedAmounts (textMapNegate senderTotals)

        receiverCids <- forA (TextMap.toList receiverTotals) \(instr, amt) -> do
          cid <- toInterfaceContractId @HoldingV2.Holding <$> create NttCoin with
            instrumentId = InstrumentId with admin = allocation.admin, id = instr
            owner = fromSome authorizerAccount.owner
            provider = authorizerAccount.provider, accountId = authorizerAccount.id, amount = amt
          pure (instr, [cid])

        archive (coerceContractId @AV2.Allocation @NttCoinAllocationV2 self)

        case arg.nextIterationFunding of
          None -> do
            leftoverCids <- returnLockedFundsToAuthorizerV2 allocation.admin authorizerAccount remaining
            pure AV2.AllocationResult with
              output = AV2.AllocationResult_Settled with nextIterationAllocationCid = None
              authorizerHoldingCids = textMapUnionWith (++) (TextMap.fromList receiverCids) leftoverCids
              meta = emptyMetadata
          Some carry -> do
            forA_ (TextMap.toList carry) \(instr, amt) -> do
              assertMsg "ntt: nextIterationFunding amounts must be positive" (amt > 0.0)
              assertMsg ("ntt: nextIterationFunding for " <> instr <> " exceeds what remains after this round's spend")
                (amt <= fromOptional 0.0 (TextMap.lookup instr remaining))
            let trueLeftover = textMapUnionWith (+) remaining (textMapNegate carry)
            leftoverCids <- returnLockedFundsToAuthorizerV2 allocation.admin authorizerAccount trueLeftover
            nextCid <- toInterfaceContractId @AV2.Allocation <$> create this with
              lockedAmounts = TextMap.filter (> 0.0) carry
              originalAllocationCid = Some (fromOptional self originalAllocationCid)
              numIterations = numIterations + 1
            pure AV2.AllocationResult with
              output = AV2.AllocationResult_Settled with nextIterationAllocationCid = Some nextCid
              authorizerHoldingCids = textMapUnionWith (++) (TextMap.fromList receiverCids) leftoverCids
              meta = emptyMetadata

      allocation_cancelImpl self arg = do
        assertMsg "ntt: Allocation_Cancel requires either executors jointly or admin alone"
          (sameGroup arg.actors settlement.executors || sameGroup arg.actors [allocation.admin])
        archive (coerceContractId @AV2.Allocation @NttCoinAllocationV2 self)
        cids <- returnLockedFundsToAuthorizerV2 allocation.admin authorizerAccount lockedAmounts
        pure AV2.AllocationResult with
          output = AV2.AllocationResult_Cancelled, authorizerHoldingCids = cids, meta = emptyMetadata

      allocation_withdrawImpl self arg = do
        -- Unilateral by the authorizer account's owner alone (matching the
        -- interface's own "account parties of the authorizer" language as a
        -- permission grant, not a joint requirement) -- mirrors the pre-Phase-2
        -- behavior for basic accounts exactly. This assertMsg is the real
        -- authorization gate: 'self's own signatories (admin + owner +
        -- provider, if any) are ambiently available inside this choice body
        -- regardless of what 'arg.actors' contains, so without this check any
        -- caller with self-authority as some actor could trigger a withdraw
        -- (still benign -- funds only ever return to the rightful authorizer
        -- account -- but not one this choice's own controller list prevents).
        assertMsg "ntt: Allocation_Withdraw requires the authorizer account owner's authority"
          (fromSome authorizerAccount.owner `elem` arg.actors)
        when allocation.committed $ case allocation.settlementDeadline of
          Some deadline -> do
            now <- getTime
            assertMsg "ntt: committed allocation cannot be withdrawn before its settlement deadline"
              (now > deadline)
          None -> abort "ntt: committed allocation with no settlement deadline cannot be unilaterally withdrawn -- use Allocation_Cancel"
        archive (coerceContractId @AV2.Allocation @NttCoinAllocationV2 self)
        cids <- returnLockedFundsToAuthorizerV2 allocation.admin authorizerAccount lockedAmounts
        pure AV2.AllocationResult with
          output = AV2.AllocationResult_Withdrawn, authorizerHoldingCids = cids, meta = emptyMetadata

      allocation_settleExtraObservers _ = []
      allocation_cancelExtraObservers _ = []
      allocation_withdrawExtraObservers _ = []
